Z||000008||Monkeyman||01-23-2000||12:48 PM||||He wanted to crack a joke but he was a little intimidated by all of this.  I gave him the print out of everything you guys said so far.  Here's his responses:<P>kong--I had to explain to him what a Fieroite was.  He thought that "yard ape" was one of the funniest things he'd ever heard.<P>Cliff--He still can't believe that he has over 700 new friends.  He wondered if he could invite everyone to a sledding party.  I said no.  (Unless someone other than me would like to foot the bill!)<P>four50four--Thank you.<P>Sage--He said that he plans to have my Fiero next year some time (I think not!).  He also said that he would help me fix the interior real soon "as soon as soccer is done.  And then I have maybe baseball and Scouts is doing something one weekend and I have to go over to Mikes house (no idea who Mike is) for some Legomaniac stuff.  Maybe after that.  OK, Dad?"  That's what he said.  Word for word.<P>Cooter--My wonderful son (something like that! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) said (and I quote), "Yeah, Dad!  You're funny lookin'."<P>Sorry for the book, but he wanted to respond to everyone.  He was being polite and didn't want to leave anyone out or offend anyone.||||reg||1
